  <h2>The "× Capacity" Problem</h2>
  <p>Anthropic's multiplier (5×, 20×) applies to <em>session capacity</em> — an internal metric combining message count, context window usage, and compute allocation — not to a published token number. This means:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>No contractual token floor:</strong> Unlike Alibaba's Token Pro (12k credits/5h, 40k/7d), Anthropic guarantees no minimum token allocation.</li>
    <li><strong>Burst vs sustained:</strong> Max 20x excels at short, intense bursts (e.g., a 4-hour refactoring sprint). Sustained 24/7 load will hit dynamic throttling.</li>
    <li><strong>Model mixing:</strong> Capacity is shared across Opus 5, Sonnet 5, Fable 5, Haiku 4.5. Heavy Opus usage consumes capacity faster than Sonnet.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>API-Equivalent Valuation</h2>
  <p>To compare subscription vs API spend, estimate the weekly API-equivalent value:</p>
  <p style="background:#101726;padding:12px;border-radius:6px;font-family:monospace;color:#7AAFFF;text-align:center;">
    Weekly API Equivalent ≈ (Monthly Subscription / 4.33) × Capacity Multiplier × Utilization Factor
  </p>
  <p>At 80% utilization:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Pro: ($20/4.33) × 1 × 0.8 ≈ <strong>$3.70/week</strong> (but Opus access is limited — real value ~$25–50)</li>
    <li>Max 5x: ($100/4.33) × 5 × 0.8 ≈ <strong>$92/week</strong> (real value ~$125–250 with Opus access)</li>
    <li>Max 20x: ($200/4.33) × 20 × 0.8 ≈ <strong>$739/week</strong> (real value ~$500–1,100)</li>
  </ul>
  <p><strong>Key insight:</strong> Max 20x at $200/mo delivers ~12–27× its subscription cost in API-equivalent value <em>if fully utilized</em>. The risk is underutilization — an idle Max 20x seat costs $200/mo for $0 value.</p>

