  <h2>Hidden Costs & Gotchas</h2>
  <h3>1. No API Access Included</h3>
  <p>Max plans cover <em>only</em> interactive Claude Code and web chat. Any CI/CD pipeline, automated PR review bot, or backend service calling Anthropic API is billed separately at standard rates (Opus 5: $15/M in, $75/M out).</p>

  <h3>2. Prompt Caching Not Exposed</h3>
  <p>API users get 90% cache-read discount ($1.50/M vs $15/M). Max plan users cannot explicitly control or measure prompt cache hits — the dynamic pool manages it opaquely.</p>

  <h3>3. No Off-Peak Discount</h3>
  <p>Unlike Alibaba Token Pro (0.2× credits 22:00–08:00 UTC+8), Anthropic offers no time-of-day pricing. A Max 20x seat costs $200/mo whether used at 2 PM or 2 AM.</p>

  <h3>4. Account-Level Pooling Risk</h3>
  <p>Max 20x capacity is drawn from a <em>shared account pool</em>. One engineer's runaway agent swarm can throttle the entire team's Max 20x seats. No per-seat guarantees exist.</p>

  <h2>FinOps Recommendation</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Start with Max 5x for all daily coders.</strong> $100/mo × 5 engineers = $500/mo. Monitor actual limit-hit frequency for 30 days.</li>
    <li><strong>Upgrade individuals to Max 20x only when data shows:</strong> (a) hitting Max 5x limits >3×/week, (b) measurable productivity loss from throttling, (c) API overflow spend >$100/mo for that engineer.</li>
    <li><strong>Track "subscription utilization" monthly:</strong> (sessions used / estimated capacity) × 100. Target >60% on Max 5x, >40% on Max 20x.</li>
    <li><strong>Keep API budget separate.</strong> Subscriptions ≠ API. Budget API spend for automation, batch, and backend workloads independently.</li>
  </ol>

